00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:05.910 align:start position:0%
 
hi  my name is sandeep gupta and i'm a  product manager in the tensorflow team  in google  today i'll talk about tensorflow  enterprise and how it can help you in  building and deploying  your ml workloads with tensorflow on gcp  machine learning is transforming every  aspect of our lives  and developers and enterprises are using  ml to build impactful solutions  that drive business value tensorflow is  one of the most widely used production  ready frameworks for machine learning  and it's open sourced by google so that  everyone can take advantage  of these powerful tools but if you are  an enterprise  trying to use ml there are some  challenges you may face  new tensorflow open source releases come  out several times a year  and you may have business reasons to  stay on an older version longer  in this case you would want that  critical patches  fixes and enhancements be available in  these older versions  second cloud provides the ability to  build and deploy ml with the performance  and scalability that cloud offers  this can be difficult as it may require  a lot of manual configuration and setup  to make sure that you get the best out  of your infrastructure  investment and lastly you expect  prioritized and trusted support  we designed tensorflow enterprise with  the goals of addressing these types of  challenges when it comes to  enterprise grade ml tensorflow  enterprise  is the gcp optimized experience of  tensorflow  it consists of three main pillars  first is performance and the ability to  handle  cloud scale data and models tensorflow  enterprise  includes optimizations to help you get  the most from your data pipelines and ml  model training  on gcp second is manageability  while solving your business problem you  do not want to spend your time and  energy  creating and maintaining the software  environment and managing all the  machines in your cluster  you just want to focus on the core  business logic of your ml problem that  matters to your business  tensorflow enterprise makes it easier to  build and run ml workloads  with these managed services and lastly  tfe releases come with long term support  which provides back porting of critical  patches and fixes  so we'll look at all three of these in  more detail now  let's start by looking at cloud scale  performance first  so with tensorflow enterprise we compile  and ship  a special build of tensorflow which is  optimized for google cloud  infrastructure  it is built on open source tensorflow  but it contains  add-ons with additional runtime  optimizations and i o optimizations  which are specific for google cloud  machines and services  to help improve performance let's take a  look at an example  so this is a code snippet that you can  use to train a model  with potentially a large training data  set in google cloud storage  cloud storage is gcp's file storage  where you might maintain  terabytes of training data as you see  this code snippet is no different from  your typical tensorflow code  written with the tf.data api except that  the path to the files  points to your gcs bucket under the hood  tensorflow enterprise  built contains optimized i o readers to  make this performant  with google cloud storage here's another  example  where we read our training data set from  a big query table  bigquery is gcp's sql based data  warehouse  where you might maintain a business  intelligence data lake  with hundreds of millions of rows in  many tables  and you might want to train your models  from all this data  here we are specifying the table to read  from  the columns to read and their data types  and several other specifications  similar to the standard tf data api and  we are performing additional  transformations  such as batching and shuffling under the  hood  optimized i o for bigquery can read many  millions of rows in parallels  into the tensors efficiently so with  these optimizations included  you can get faster throughput in your  model training  with tensorflow enterprise here is an  example  on a recommendations data set where we  see that we get about a 30 percent  higher throughput  with tensorflow enterprise optimizations  this gain in data throughput  improves the utilization of accelerators  such as gpus  because now you are no longer  bottlenecked by io  it results in shorter wall time of  training for the same accuracy  as shown in the chart on the left the  purple graph you see here  is the gpu utilization profile with  tensorflow enterprise 1.15  on one model training example you see  that it is narrower in time  indicating shorter wall time and also  attains a higher peak  indicating higher peak utilization  compared to the orange graph  with tensorflow 1.14 which does not have  these optimizations  this better i o throughput helps reduce  the cost of training  also with networking optimizations to  nickel  better performance is achieved when you  scale to large clusters of gpus  for example when training the burt large  model for nlp problems  on a 64 gpu cluster we see about a 30  speed up with these improvements built  in  so we have seen some optimizations for  better scale and performance on gcp  in tensorflow enterprise now let's take  a look at how tensorflow enterprise  makes it easy to build ml  through managed services we deliver  tensorflow enterprise through a managed  environment  these are in the form of deep learning  vm images and deep learning container  images  where the environment is pre-configured  on top of a standard linux box  and made available to you what makes  this convenient  is that it pre-installs the tensorflow  enterprise build  together with all the dependencies  including device drivers  common dependency packages and  configurations  to other services on google cloud this  means that you no longer have to think  about  installing all the right packages and  drivers with correct combination of  versions  or wrangle with all of their  configurations  and support for all google compute  engine security features  such as customer managed encryption keys  and vpc  is built in right out of the box because  these are packaged pm and container  images  you have many choices for deploying them  and using them on the cloud  to get started you pick the tensorflow  enterprise image  and the desired resources such as the  machine type and the accelerator choice  and you start the virtual machine all  with one line of command  then you can ssh into the machine that  has tensorflow enterprise installed  with all dependencies and device drivers  pre-configured  and you can start using tensorflow if  you prefer a notebook environment  jupyter lab is hosted and already  started on the vm  so you can go to the browser and start  writing code  in a notebook once you have a  satisfactory model  after running some experiments now you  can train your model with the full scale  of your enterprise data it may not fit  into one machine  and you may want to take advantage of  distributed training  for large scale of data and models  gcp's ai platform training is a managed  service  for serverless training that takes care  of distributed training clusters  and provisioning of compute resources  more importantly it drives the same  tensorflow enterprise container  which has the same environment as you  have developed the model with  so you can be confident that your model  just trains  with the full scale of data on ai  platform training  here we see an example of how to do this  you create a custom container starting  with a tensorflow enterprise base image  overlay this with your model training  code  then you issue one command to start  serverless training on gcp  in this example we are using 10 workers  for our distributed training cluster  with 8 v1 v100 gpus attached to each  this brings up the distributed training  cluster with tensorflow enterprise  optimizations included  very soon cloud ai platform training  will use these tfe images  as the default runtime so you will not  have to import  a tfe container manually as shown here  now that you have trained your model in  full enterprise scale  it is time to make it an end-to-end  pipeline  to continue running in production this  can be done  using gcp's ai platform pipelines which  are built with tensorflow extended or  tfx  platform pipelines is hosted on google  kubernetes engine  so it can also drive the same tensorflow  enterprise container image  so that all the optimizations are still  included and you can be confident that  your pipeline  trains the same way as your notebook  code  in addition to managed training and  hosted pipelines there are other  additions that make tensorflow run  better on gcp with tensorflow enterprise  add-ons  let me show you two examples first  tensorflow cloud repositories apis  allow you to easily go from debugging  and training your keras and tensorflow  code  in a local environment to distributed  training  in the cloud to use this simply add the  tf cloud run api call  to your keras model training code it  will take care of adding the right tf  distribution strategy  based on the cluster configuration that  you provide and a training job will be  triggered  on jcp using the cloud ai platform apis  hybrid parameter tuning is an important  step in fine tuning and optimizing your  model  you can use the keras tuner api  conveniently within keras  to use hyper parameter tuning in your  model training  cloud tuner is gcp's implementation of  the keras tuner api  it is fully api compatible with grass  tuner and uses gcp's optimizer search  algorithm under the hood  to run the hyper parameter tuning these  add-ons  are part of the standard build of  tensorflow enterprise  and make your journey from offline  experimentation  to cloud scale implementation easier  now that we have seen cloud scale  performance and cloud integrated managed  services  let's talk about enterprise grade  support that comes with tensorflow  enterprise  key aspect of this is long-term support  open source tensorflow comes with a one  year of maintenance window  for tensorflow enterprise we extend that  and commit to providing  three years of support that includes  critical bug fixes  and security patches and optionally back  porting  important feature enhancements from  future releases  based on customer needs and demand this  means that you can rest assured  that you can upgrade tensorflow versions  based on your business's timelines as of  today we support both tensorflow 1.x  and 2.x with tensorflow enterprise  long-term support  here's a great example of what long-term  support can mean for you in practice  nvidia recently launched their a100  family of gpus  which brings significant performance  improvements in collaboration with  nvidia  we have updated the tensorflow  enterprise 1.15  and 2.1 deep learning vm images and  added support for cuda 11 kodi n8  and the new tensorflow 32 data format  to help your code take advantage of the  a100 architecture  these tensorflow enterprise versions are  the only official builds of tensorflow  115 and 2.1  with this support built in before this  lands in the mainline  open source releases you can become an  early user of these gpus on gcp  with these pre-built images getting  started is really easy  with this example gcloud command line as  shown here  where we create a tensorflow enterprise  2.1 vm  which supports a100 gpus you can learn  more about these gpus in our cloud  accelerator session  before closing let me share what lies  ahead  for tensorflow enterprise we are excited  to keep working tightly together  between google cloud and the tensorflow  teams  as being the creators and experts of  both we plan to provide further  optimizations and enhancements  to tensorflow on google cloud better  monitoring and debugging capabilities  to fourier tensorflow code and  integrations  into google cloud tooling we're also  looking at smoother integration between  tensorflow's high-level apis such as  kiras and the training services  as well as more managed services such as  enterprise version of tensorboard.dev  and integrated experiment management and  tracking  for a seamless and joyful developer  experience  i hope i've been able to show you how  tensorflow enterprise  can help your business use ml and  tensorflow on gcp  to get started visit this link shown  here and check out all the documentation  and resources  on behalf of the tensorflow enterprise  team i would like to thank you for  listening  thank you  you

